Description: software_isp: report a luminance-gradient focus metric
 The CPU statistics accumulate the absolute difference between
 horizontally adjacent luminance samples of each statistics line
 (focusSum, focusSamples in SwIspStats), and the simple soft IPA reports
 it as the FocusFoM metadata control.
 .
 Patch 2/4 of the libcamera autofocus series of iceland-mainline
 990a0597, a cherry-pick of commit
 9afba3cd3da3c84fc6acabf24aa6c7092c0a641f.
 .
 Ported by hand to 0.7.0: 0.7.1 accumulates statistics per worker thread
 (a stats array passed to every line function, summed in finishFrame()),
 0.7.0 accumulates into the single SwStatsCpu::stats_ that finishFrame()
 copies whole to the shared buffer. The line macros therefore write to
 stats_, startFrame() clears the two new fields of stats_, and the
 finishFrame() hunk is dropped. The metric itself is unchanged. The
 SwIspStats layout changes, so libcamera0.7 and libcamera-ipa from this
 build must be installed together.
